  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Monitoring, Evaluation, Learning Partnerships, and Technical Advisory</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This component supports the Asia-Pacific Regional Governance Programme&#x2019;s monitoring, evaluation and learning (MEL) and provision of technical advisory services, delivered through ODA-eligible grants or consultancy arrangements, with a primary focus on strengthening governance, institutional effectiveness, and evidence-based policy engagement in partner countries. It also funds a learning partnership with The Asia Foundation to generate targeted analytical outputs&#x2014;including regional diagnostics and country case studies&#x2014;alongside tailored political economy analysis (PEA), capacity-building support and training for country posts, and facilitated learning exchanges; all aimed at enhancing the effectiveness, contextual relevance, and strategic design of governance programming in line with ODA objectives of promoting sustainable development, inclusive institutions, and accountable governance systems.</narrative>
  </description>
